    <briefdescription>
<para>Compile-time constraints tying generic API code to domain types. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares four C++20 &quot;concepts&quot; — named conditions that a type must satisfy before a template will accept it. Each one checks that a type is a particular domain class (<ref refid="controller_8hpp_1af928d8b9ced02f7387b9b56ed3877b11" kindref="member">Client</ref>, <ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref>, <ref refid="classCase" kindref="compound">Case</ref> or <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref>) or something derived from it. The classes themselves are only forward-declared here, so this header stays light and does not pull in heavy definitions. The checks happen during compilation, so a wrong type produces a clear compile error instead of a crash at runtime.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: The controllers are templates that work with several related entity types. These concepts act as a safety gate: they stop someone instantiating a controller with an unrelated type (for example, a std::string) by rejecting it at compile time. This keeps the generic API code flexible but still tied to the real domain objects. It is a header-only helper included where those generic templates are declared.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>C++20 concepts / constraints: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/constraints">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/constraints</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::is_base_of: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_base_of">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_base_of</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Forward declarations: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/class#Forward_declaration">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/class#Forward_declaration</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
